{
  "original_id": "primary-20260914-brugidou-positivity",
  "archive_id": "BW2-PR20260914-brugidou_positivity",
  "title": "Positive initial coefficients and a positivity region for Brugidou's hook polynomials",
  "batch_label": "primary",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "Let phi_q(e_j)=q^(j(j-1)/2)/j! and define J_lambda by phi_q(m_lambda)=(1-q)^(n-r) q^nu(lambda) J_lambda/((n-1)! product_j a_j(lambda)!), where n=|lambda|, r=l(lambda), nu(lambda)=sum_i(i-1)lambda_i and a_j(lambda) is the multiplicity of j. For all integers a>=2,b>=0, set K_(a,b)=J_(a,1^b)/b!, d=binom(a-1,2)+(a-1)b and D=binom(a-2,2). Then K_(a,b) is in Z[q], and [q^k]K_(a,b)>0 for every integer 0<=k<=min(d,2b+3). If b>=max(0,ceil((D-4)/2)), every coefficient from degree 0 through d is strictly positive. With the established one-row cases b=0, this covers all hooks with 2<=a<=6. No assertion of optimality, log-concavity, or full all-partition positivity is made.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
